## AI Agent Reasoning

### Context

Issue #1 was revised from basic multiple-depth support to importing the common
Windows BMP families into the existing RGB-only PixelMatrix while reporting
discarded color information through Bitmap::isLossy().

### Decisions Made

- Parse fixed-width little-endian fields instead of native structs so malformed
  files, host alignment, and host endianness cannot corrupt interpretation.
- Decode into temporary state and commit atomically so rejected files never
  expose partial pixels or stale lossiness.
- Implement BI_RLE4 and BI_RLE8 directly because Microsoft documents them and
  they require no codec dependency; keep embedded JPEG/PNG explicitly out of
  scope.
- Preserve stored RGB values when alpha is discarded. Mark the import lossy
  only when at least one declared alpha sample is non-opaque.
- Preserve numeric V4/V5 RGB values without color-profile conversion and mark
  meaningful ignored color metadata as lossy.

### Trade-offs

- Known DIB header sizes are allowlisted rather than guessing unknown layouts.
- Input and decoded-pixel caps reject extreme files in exchange for bounded
  memory exposure.
- Save output remains 24-bpp BI_RGB to preserve the existing public contract.

